<!--
This file configures the different items in the game
Items can be sprites or models
If the model tag is present the texture will be the texture for that model
If the model tag is present the facing tags are ignored
The textures are looked from the same folder than material textures are. See @folder in materials.xml

@item This configures one item
	The item must have one of the following:
	@name This is the doom editor number name from https://zdoom.org/wiki/Standard_editor_numbers
	@number This the doom editor number

	@texture This is the file name of the image to use as a texture.
	@model [optional] This is the file name of the fbx file to load the mesh from.

	@size [default: 1] Size of the collision box
	@height [default: 1] Height of the collision box

	@renderwidth [optional] Size when drawing. If not set, texture width is used
	@renderheight [optional] Size when drawing. If not set, texture height is used

	The item can look different from different directions
	If no facings are configured the whole texture is used for all the facings
	@facing This configures a facing
		@direction [attribute] The facing, seen from player. Values are front, frontleft, frontright,left,
		right, backleft, back, backright
		The section of the texture used for this facing can be configured in pixels
		@x The x of lower left point of the section
		@y The y of lower left point of the section
		@w The width of the section
		@h The height of the section
-->
<items>
	<folder>assets</folder>

	<item>
		<name>BlueCard</name>
		<texture>BlueCard.png</texture>
		<size>32</size>
		<height>32</height>
	</item>
</items>
